  "generated_text": "1. **Determine the diameter of the sphere:**\n   Since the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube. Therefore, the diameter of the sphere is 6 inches.\n\n2. **Calculate the radius of the sphere:**\n   The radius of the sphere is half of the diameter. Thus, the radius \\(r\\) is \\(\\frac{6}{2} = 3\\) inches.\n\n3. **Calculate the volume of the sphere:**\n   The volume \\(V\\) of a sphere is given by the formula \\(V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\). Substituting \\(r = 3\\) inches into the formula:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (3)^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\times 27 = \\frac{108}{3}\\pi = 36\\pi\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   The volume of the inscribed sphere is \\(36\\pi\\) cubic inches.\n\n   \\boxed{36\\pi}",
